// The following oscillator models have spice model, which is idealized. Please be aware of the fact that the real model 
// might work in similar way in some circuits, but also will work differently in other circuits. For example:
// - The circuits here have resistances between the positive and negative connection of ca.1MegaOhm, but in case of CMOS-Technology, the real components may have an even larger resistance. Therefor the current consumption may be even lower.
// - The circuits here have an idealized rise and fall time, which means that the switch time between high and low voltage here is only the time step of the simulation. Real components often also have a small rise and fall time of just a few nanoseconds, but in some cases even this might be relevant, or some real components might have other rise and fall times. Also the real rise and fall curve might not be an ideal straight line as in the model, but may have the form of a loading curve or may have an overshoot.
// -> So for the users: Please be aware of the differences between the real components and the idealized model
// -> So for the jurists: this library is presented AS IS. We are not liable of any consequences resulting from it in any way
